{
  "title": "Second declension: masculine nouns",
  "note": "Most second-declension nouns end in -ος and are masculine. λόγος: singular λόγος, λόγου, λόγῳ, λόγον, vocative λόγε; plural λόγοι, λόγων, λόγοις, λόγους. Dictionaries give the nominative, the genitive ending and the article: λόγος, -ου, ὁ. A long final syllable (-ου, -ῳ, -ων, -οις, -ους) can pull the accent forward: ἄνθρωπος, ἀνθρώπου.",
